---
import Button from "@rottensea/ds-personal-website/components/buttons/Button.astro";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { parseSetup } from "../scripts/windows-setup.ts";
import { FILES } from "../scripts/windows-setup-files.ts";

// The lists below come from the scripts' own files, the same ones the zip packs, so the page
// can't drift from what people download.
const scripts = parseSetup(FILES);
const count = scripts.reduce((sum, script) => sum + script.items.length, 0);
const about: Record<string, string> = {
  "1-Offline.ps1":
    "Before going online, from Terminal (Admin): the settings the guide changes by hand, then the WinUtil tweaks it recommends. Turning off UAC comes first.",
  "2-Online.ps1":
    "Once online, from a normal terminal: the developer environment. Needs the internet."
};

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
const file = "windows-setup.zip";
const download = `${base}windows-setup/${file}`;
// Button types its attributes as a button's, which have no `download`, so it goes in through a spread.
const saveAs: Record<string, string> = { download: file };

const guide = "https://archive.rottenth.cafe/system/windows/";
const title = "Windows setup";
const description =
  "Two PowerShell scripts that apply the settings, tweaks and developer tools from a Windows 11 install guide.";
---

<Page
  title={title}
  description={description}
  top
>
  <article>
    <header class="intro">
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="lede">{description}</p>
      <p class="meta">PowerShell 5.1 · Windows 11 · {count} changes in {scripts.length} scripts</p>
      <Button
        href={download}
        {...saveAs}
        iconLeft="download"
      >
        Download {file}
      </Button>
    </header>

    <section class="prose">
      <p>
        The scripts go with the <a href={guide}>Windows install guide</a> (in Chinese): the first does
        the settings the guide changes by hand and the WinUtil tweaks the guide recommends, without
        running WinUtil; the second sets up the developer environment. Each lists every change first
        and asks once before applying them. Nothing is backed up and there is no undo, so read the
        list before you say yes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Run it</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Download the zip and extract it (right-click it, <strong>Extract All</strong>).</li>
        <li>Before going online, press Win+X, open <strong>Terminal (Admin)</strong>, go to the <code>windows-setup</code> folder and run <code>powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\1-Offline.ps1</code>. Without administrator rights it stops and changes nothing.</li>
        <li>Read the list, say yes, and restart when it's done: turning off UAC takes effect after the restart.</li>
        <li>Once online, open a normal terminal in the same folder and run <code>powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\2-Online.ps1</code>, if you want the developer environment.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>What they change</h2>
      {
        scripts.map((script) => (
          <section class="group">
            <h3><code>{script.file}</code></h3>
            <p>{about[script.file]}</p>
            <dl>
              {script.items.map((item) => (
                <div class="option">
                  <dt>
                    <span>{item.title}</span>
                  </dt>
                  <dd>{item.description}</dd>
                </div>
              ))}
            </dl>
          </section>
        ))
      }
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>What it leaves to you</h2>
      <p>
        Drivers, startup apps, display scale and refresh rate, theme, device name, languages,
        uninstalling apps and arranging Start depend on your computer and taste, so the guide does
        them by hand. So are a few settings that have no registry value or command known to work, such
        as the Snap options and the touchpad's three-finger tap.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>
        The WinUtil tweaks in <code>1-Offline.ps1</code> follow the tweaks in Chris Titus Tech's
        <a href="https://github.com/ChrisTitusTech/winutil">Windows Utility</a>, MIT license; the
        zip includes its notice.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Page>

<style>
  article {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    width: min(100%, var(--container-reading));
  }

  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  h1 {
    font: var(--display-md-weight) var(--display-md-size) / var(--display-md-lh) var(--display-md-family);
    letter-spacing: var(--display-md-ls);
    color: var(--text-ink);
  }

  .lede {
    font: var(--title-sm-weight) var(--title-sm-size) / var(--title-sm-lh) var(--title-sm-family);
    color: var(--text-body-strong);
  }

  .meta {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    font: var(--caption-weight) var(--caption-size) / var(--caption-lh) var(--caption-family);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    font: var(--body-md-weight) var(--body-md-size) / var(--body-md-lh) var(--body-md-family);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font: var(--title-lg-weight) var(--title-lg-size) / var(--title-lg-lh) var(--title-lg-family);
    color: var(--text-ink);
  }

  h3 {
    font: var(--title-md-weight) var(--title-md-size) / var(--title-md-lh) var(--title-md-family);
    color: var(--text-ink);
  }

  ol {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    padding-left: 1.5em;
    list-style: decimal;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--text-link);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--text-body-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  code {
    font: var(--code-weight) var(--code-size) / var(--code-lh) var(--code-family);
    padding: 0.1em 0.3em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    background: var(--surface-code);
  }

  .group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  dl {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--surface-card);
  }

  .option {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xxs);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
  }

  .option + .option {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-soft);
  }

  dt {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--text-ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  dd {
    font: var(--body-sm-weight) var(--body-sm-size) / var(--body-sm-lh) var(--body-sm-family);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
